      "closure_rationale": "The canonical unsigned fraction invariant is proved with Euclid remainder preservation and descent. Zero normalizes to0/1; Fibonacci47/46 takes45remainder steps, with a derivation obligation beyond observation. Public struct construction does not prevent later alias corruption. The consuming boundary validates canonical form; the actual incomplete private type rejects ordinary field access in GCC/Clang C17 but cannot authenticate arbitrary forged pointers or establish static refinement safety. Actual retained er_refine is imported by checked public consumers, naive addition and cancellation-based addition. Both fields publish together after admission. The separate opaque hosted comparison validates before explicit raw allocation, preserves empty owner on failure, and empties ownership before its matching release. It does not silently claim the T66 typed-cell allocator is a compatible raw-storage provider. Six C17 profiles execute six anchors, eight compiled semantic controls and six compiling-stub rejections. Per profile, an independent Python Fraction/integer oracle checks65585unsigned normalizations,1024consumers,5204additions,65578signed normalizations,8651signed additions,70signed consumers and47Fibonacci pairs. Exact native compile commands and negative opaque translation evidence are pinned; sanitizers are not substitutes for the integer range derivations. The required changed signed variant uses a positive uint32 denominator and separate unsigned magnitude, never -INT32_MIN or abs(INT32_MIN). Cancellation-based addition derives bounded uint64 intermediates, complete representable canonical results and unchanged refusal. Opposite signs subtract magnitudes; exact zero is0/1. Compare the naive narrower intermediate policy without claiming equivalent admitted contracts. Signed truncation and INT32_MIN construction/consumption run in every profile; independent delayed learner work remains unassessed. Bounded author support only."
